<article class="env-example" id="DB19D2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/DB19D2">Example <span data-tag="DB19D2">8.2.9.28</span>.</a> Let $\mathbf{A}$ be a simplicial model category, so that we have a left Quillen bifunctor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \otimes : \mathbf{A}\times \sSet \rightarrow \mathbf{A}. \]
</div>
  <p> The coend construction determines a left Quillen bifunctor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \int _{\cDelta }: \Fun ( \cDelta , \mathbf{A}) \times \Fun ( \cDelta ^{op}, \sSet ) \rightarrow \mathbf{A}. \]
</div>
  <p> where $\Fun (\cDelta , \mathbf{A})$ and $\Fun ( \cDelta ^{op}, \sSet )$ are both endowed with the Reedy model structure. In particular, if we fix a cosimplicial object $X^{\bullet } \in \Fun (\cDelta , \mathbf{A})$ which is Reedy cofibrant, then forming the coend against $X^{\bullet }$ determines a left Quillen functor from the category of bisimplicial sets (with the Reedy model structure, which coincides with the injective model structure by Example <a href="/tag/F9111E" data-tag="F9111E">8.2.9.21</a>) to $\mathbf{A}$. </p>
